# condor_submit_dag poet_ts.dag : HMI cell filling factors at the times of the PoET disk-integrated time series
# (poet_ts_jdb.csv, 3237 exposures, 46 days of poet_ts_days.txt), 4096 px, 60 rings, hmi.M_45s and
# hmi.Ic_noLimbDark_720s, thresholds of CAUP/poet_sdo_s1d_a.ipynb (parameters_poet_ts.txt: noise_th 8, B_th 24, I_th 0.87,
# A_th 10, mu_area 0.1, plage), everything in ${BASE}/poet_ts (settings_poet_ts.sh):
#   1. one job per day: every exposure takes the closest 720 s continuum (and the 45 s magnetogram closest to it),
#      downloaded from JSOC, identified and deleted (poet_ts_day.sub)
#   2. the filling factors over all the days: ident/<set label>/ and exposures.csv (poet_ts_collect.sub)
# The simulation runs in CAUP/poet_sdo_timeseries.ipynb (copy ident/ and exposures.csv to poet/output/sdo_timeseries).
# Test first on 3 days: condor_submit poet_ts_day.sub with poet_ts_days.txt cut to 3 days.
JOB days    poet_ts_day.sub
JOB collect poet_ts_collect.sub
PARENT days CHILD collect
SCRIPT POST days /bin/true
